---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Prompt from '../components/Prompt.astro';

const steps = [
    { short: 'write', text: 'I start by writing concepts down by hand so I can actively reconstruct what I am learning rather than just copy it.' },
    { short: 'explain', text: 'I explain the idea to myself in simple language, almost as if I were teaching someone else.' },
    { short: 'struggle', text: 'If I get stuck on a proof, derivation, algorithm, or concept, I spend time trying to fully understand it on my own before moving on.' },
    { short: 'mark', text: 'If I still cannot resolve it, I mark it as unfinished and return to it later with more focus.', note: 'The weak point becomes the target of my next review.' },
    { short: 'resolve', text: 'After reviewing everything once, I revisit the difficult parts, resolve them, and then rebuild the topic again with a clearer structure.' },
];
const ordinals = ['First', 'Second', 'Third', 'Fourth', 'Fifth'];

// Nodes of the loop diagram, evenly spaced on a circle (starting at the top).
const R = 70, CX = 110, CY = 100;
const nodes = steps.map((s, i) => {
    const a = -Math.PI / 2 + (i / steps.length) * Math.PI * 2;
    return { ...s, x: CX + R * Math.cos(a), y: CY + R * Math.sin(a) };
});
---

<Base title="Learning Strategy" description="How Sungjun Lee studies: optimization, the Feynman Technique, and a loop called Fold and Resolve.">
    <header>
        <h1 class="page-title">Learning Strategy</h1>
        <div class="subtitle">Optimization &amp; Study Habits</div>
    </header>

    <section class="section">
        <Prompt path="~/learning" command="cat philosophy.txt" />
        <blockquote class="thesis">Learning, to me, is a process of optimization through reconstruction.</blockquote>
        <div class="content">
            <p>Inspired by scientific thinking and the <strong>Feynman Technique</strong>, I do not study by simply rereading material until it feels familiar.</p>
            <p>Instead, I rebuild concepts in my own words, test whether I can explain them clearly, and use moments of confusion as signals of where my understanding is weak.</p>
            <p>When I encounter a difficult idea, I isolate it, return to it deliberately, and refine it until it becomes something I can truly use.</p>
            <p>In this way, I treat studying less as memorization and more as <strong>debugging thought</strong>—a cycle of building, testing, correcting, and improving.</p>
            <p>My learning strategy is not about spending the most time, but about finding the most effective path to real understanding.</p>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
        <Prompt path="~/learning" command="cat scientist_methods.md" />
        <div class="content">
            <p>The study methods that influence me most are rooted in how scientists think:</p>
            <ol class="methods">
                <li><strong>Optimization:</strong> finding the most effective path to understanding under limited time and energy.</li>
                <li><strong>Feynman Technique:</strong> testing real understanding by explaining ideas in simple and clear language.</li>
                <li><strong>Scientific Iteration:</strong> treating confusion and mistakes not as failure, but as feedback for improvement.</li>
            </ol>
            <p>These approaches matter to me because they prioritize <strong>clarity</strong>, <strong>structure</strong>, and <strong>durable understanding</strong> over superficial familiarity.</p>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
        <Prompt path="~/learning" command="cat fold_and_resolve.md" />
        <p class="content">Below is the study method that feels most natural to me, which I think of as <strong>Fold and Resolve</strong>:</p>

        <div class="fold">
            <svg class="loop" viewBox="0 0 220 200" role="img" aria-label="Fold and Resolve: a loop of write, explain, struggle, mark, resolve, and back to write.">
                <circle class="loop-ring" cx={CX} cy={CY} r={R} />
                {nodes.map((n, i) => (
                    <g class="loop-node" data-step={i}>
                        <circle cx={n.x} cy={n.y} r="16" />
                        <text x={n.x} y={n.y + 4} text-anchor="middle">{i + 1}</text>
                        <text class="loop-label" x={n.x} y={n.y + (n.y < CY ? -22 : 30)} text-anchor="middle">{n.short}</text>
                    </g>
                ))}
            </svg>

            <ol class="steps">
                {steps.map((s, i) => (
                    <li class="step" data-step={i} tabindex="0">
                        <span class="step-n">{ordinals[i]}</span>
                        <span>{s.text} {s.note && <span class="step-note">{s.note}</span>}</span>
                    </li>
                ))}
            </ol>
        </div>

        <p class="content outro">For me, learning is not the passive accumulation of information, but an active cycle of testing, refining, and strengthening understanding until it becomes clear, connected, and usable.</p>
    </section>
</Base>

<style>
    .page-title { font-family: var(--font-header); }

    .thesis {
        margin: 6px 0 16px;
        padding: 12px 16px;
        border-left: 3px solid var(--header-color);
        background: var(--bg-color2);
        border-radius: 0 6px 6px 0;
        color: var(--header-color);
        font-weight: bold;
    }

    .methods, .steps { list-style: none; padding: 0; }
    .methods li::before, .steps li::before { content: none; }
    .methods { counter-reset: m; }
    .methods li { counter-increment: m; }
    .methods li::before { content: counter(m) '. '; color: var(--sub-header-color); }

    .fold {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: 220px 1fr;
        gap: 12px 24px;
        align-items: center;
        margin: 12px 0;
    }

    .loop { width: 220px; height: 200px; overflow: visible; }
    .loop-ring {
        fill: none;
        stroke: var(--line-dim);
        stroke-width: 1.5;
        stroke-dasharray: 5 6;
        animation: loop-flow 6s linear infinite;
    }
    @keyframes loop-flow { to { stroke-dashoffset: -110; } }
    .loop-node circle { fill: var(--bg-color2); stroke: var(--st-color); stroke-width: 1.5; transition: fill 0.2s, stroke 0.2s; }
    .loop-node text { fill: var(--text-color); font-family: var(--font-stack); font-size: 12px; }
    .loop-node .loop-label { fill: var(--sub-header-color); font-size: 11px; }
    .loop-node.is-on circle { fill: rgba(255, 158, 100, 0.2); stroke: var(--header-color); }
    .loop-node.is-on .loop-label { fill: var(--header-color); }

    .step {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: 5.2em 1fr;
        gap: 10px;
        padding: 6px 10px;
        margin: 2px 0;
        border-radius: 6px;
        border: 1px solid transparent;
        outline: none;
    }
    .step.is-on { border-color: rgba(255, 158, 100, 0.45); background: rgba(255, 158, 100, 0.06); }
    .step-n { color: var(--st-color); font-weight: bold; }
    .step-note { color: var(--st-color); font-weight: bold; }
    .outro { margin-top: 16px; }

    @media (max-width: 700px) {
        .fold { grid-template-columns: 1fr; justify-items: center; }
    }
    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
        .loop-ring { animation: none; }
    }
</style>

<script>
    // Hovering a step lights up its node in the loop (and vice versa). With no hover, the loop cycles.
    let timer = 0;
    let current = 0;
    let held = false;

    function light(step: number | null) {
        document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement | SVGElement>('[data-step]').forEach(el =>
            el.classList.toggle('is-on', step !== null && Number(el.dataset.step) === step));
    }

    document.addEventListener('pointerover', e => {
        const el = (e.target as Element).closest?.<HTMLElement>('[data-step]');
        if (!el) return;
        held = true;
        light(Number(el.dataset.step));
    });
    document.addEventListener('pointerout', e => {
        const el = (e.target as Element).closest?.<HTMLElement>('[data-step]');
        if (el && !el.contains(e.relatedTarget as Node)) held = false;
    });
    document.addEventListener('focusin', e => {
        const el = (e.target as Element).closest?.<HTMLElement>('.step[data-step]');
        if (el) { held = true; light(Number(el.dataset.step)); }
    });

    document.addEventListener('astro:page-load', () => {
        clearInterval(timer);
        if (!document.querySelector('.loop')) return;
        const calm = matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches;
        light(0);
        if (calm) return;
        timer = window.setInterval(() => {
            if (held || !document.querySelector('.loop')) return;
            current = (current + 1) % 5;
            light(current);
        }, 1800);
    });
</script>
